+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+# [MP8] Disco Dodge 8-player support — **only spread out the spawn points, nothing else changes** (user decision, 2026-08-17)
+# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
+#
+# Diagnostic findings (probe50 + code reading) — **this minigame supports 8 players almost out of the box.**
+#   · The tile grid is laid out at runtime by `spawn_tiles()` from `tile_rows × tile_columns` and is **automatically centered on the origin**.
+#     Symbol assignment, tile picking and scoring all iterate over `tiles` and don't depend on player count.
+#   · Scoring is pure family-A placement scoring (`player_scores[dead_players[i]] = i`, the survivor gets `player_count`),
+#     so it scales with player count automatically.
+#   · No fixed-size array in the whole file is indexed by player (the spawn points are container-style, read via `get_children()`).
+#
+# ⚠️ **The real arena size and the script defaults differ by 5x** (the sixth time a literal has fooled this project).
+#   The script says `tile_rows=20 / tile_columns=12`, but **the scene overrides them to 8 / 6** → only 48 tiles.
+#   Each tile is 4.0 units → arena x∈[-16,+16], z∈[-12,+12].
+#
+# The one obvious 8-player flaw is that **the 4 vanilla spawn points are all crammed into a 4×4 m box at (±2, ±2)**,
+# while the arena is 32×24. 8 players would start stacked on that small central patch.
+#
+# **The fix** — every spawn point sits on a **tile center**, one player per tile, spreading out from the middle.
+#   Tile center grid is x = -14,-10,-6,-2,2,6,10,14   z = -10,-6,-2,2,6,10
+#   The 4 vanilla points are exactly the centers of the central 2×2 tiles (local ±2, ±2) —
+#   for 8 players we just extend that to **4×2 = 8 tiles**, x∈{-6,-2,2,6} × z∈{-2,2}, still one tile apart.
+#
+# ⚠️ **The arena was not enlarged** (on 2026-08-17 the user chose "only spread the spawn points").
+#   Enlarging the tile grid was looked into. The camera sits at (0,14.25,+17.92), pitched down 39.1°, fov 67.8,
+#   and the bottom edge of the view frustum hits the ground around z=+13.6 while the grid's near edge is already at z=+12 — **only 1.6 units of margin on the near side**.
+#   Add to `tile_columns` and the nearest row drops off the bottom of the screen. Enlarging it **means moving the camera too**.
+const MP8_MAX_PLAYERS: int = 8
+
+# ⚠️ Makes network_manager's generic spawn top-up stand aside. From here on this minigame manages its own spawn points.
+# Set to true at declaration — the generic top-up may run before _ready(), so setting it in _ready() would be too late.
+var mp8_owns_spawns: bool = true
+var mp8_player_count: int = 0
+
+
