+
+# [MP8] Logs placement/name/score at results time, purely for reconciling afterwards. No scores are touched.
+#
+# ② Scoring — **user decision 2026-08-17: keep vanilla, change nothing** (the same choice as for Chisel Gauntlet).
+# Vanilla scoring comes down to just two rules.
+#   `player_scores[dead_players[i]] = i`   — the i-th player to fall gets i points
+#   `player_scores[survivor] = player_count` — the last one standing gets the total player count
+# So 4 players = 0/1/2/**4** and 8 players = 0/1/2/3/4/5/6/**8**,
+# **there is always a 2-point jump between 1st and 2nd**, every other step is 1. The user judged that extra point a fair reward for "surviving to the end" and did not flatten it.
+#
+# ⚠️ **Known unfixed vanilla bug (the user chose to leave it in the same decision)**
+# `player_count` is the **starting player count** recorded in `spawn_players()` and is not updated on disconnect.
+# If someone disconnects mid-match, the survivor gets more points than the number of players actually in the results — a few free points.
+# Junk Platform deliberately used `dead_players.size()` instead of `player_count` to dodge exactly this.
+# To fix it, replace `:431` with `dead_players.size() + 1` (identical to vanilla when nobody disconnects).
+#
+# ⚠️ Side note — `scoring_players` is **dead code**. It is declared and `remove_player` has one
+# `erase` on it, but nothing in the file ever appends to it. Exactly the same shape as Manufacture Gun's `finished_players`.
+# It doesn't affect scoring, but don't be misled into thinking "there's another ordered array here to use".
+func _mp8_log_scores() -> void :
+
+	var rows := PackedStringArray()
+
+	for i in dead_players.size():
+		var id: int = dead_players[i]
+		rows.append("fell #%d %s %d pts" % [i + 1, _mp8_name(id), i])
+
+	for network_id in active_players.keys():
+		rows.append("survivor %s %d pts" % [_mp8_name(network_id), player_count])
+		break
+
+	print("[MP8] Disco Dodge results (%d players at start / %d fell): %s" % [
+		player_count, dead_players.size(), " | ".join(rows)
+	])
+
+
+func _mp8_name(network_id: int) -> String :
+	if players.has(network_id) and is_instance_valid(players[network_id]):
+		return String(players[network_id].player_presence.network_name)
+	return str(network_id)
+
 func finish_game():
 
 	await get_tree().create_timer(2.0).timeout
